 "policy_note": "Applied by build_plane_ref.apply_policy(). These decisions live in the TOOL, not here — a rebuild writes fresh cells and would otherwise discard them silently. See TILT_VALIDATED_RAILS / NO_TILT_CHANNELS / UNUSABLE_CELLS / SHADOW_FRAC in build_plane_ref.py for the evidence behind each.",
 "build_note": "Rebuilt 2026-09-06 with the relative-brightness (shadow) gate. Three frames from 2026-08-16_12-04-05 (stops 9/10/11, brightness 292/180/268 against that cycle median of 413 — a shadow, most likely a person at the home end on harvest day) are excluded. They passed the absolute >150 lit gate and, under FIXED bands, produced a 62.7 mm error on cell 9|2. Dropping them takes home-end cross-cycle scatter from 5-22 mm to 0.1-0.3 and closes the master file watch item on stops 9-11. plane_mm barely moved (median 0.07 mm, max 0.23) because the cross-cycle MEDIAN had already absorbed it; what changed is that sd_mm is now honest."
